Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:23:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 28/54] sampler: env-gated CPU fallback for the dist sampler
 ([TAG_SAMPLER_CPU_AUDIT])

The backend dist sampler ends with a GET_ROWS (dist_sampled_token) that
profiles at ~302us/token on gfx1151. LLAMA_DIST_CPU=1 keeps the GPU
sampler prefix (top-k/top-p) but lets the final distribution run on the
CPU over the reduced candidates, isolating that cost for A/B audit.
Default off; outputs are byte-identical either way.
---
 src/llama-sampler.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-sampler.cpp b/src/llama-sampler.cpp
index d2d95c88b18..8dd0d0b8e82 100644
--- a/src/llama-sampler.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-sampler.cpp
@@ -1273,7 +1273,11 @@ static bool llama_sampler_dist_backend_init(
         uint32_t                     n_outputs_max_per_seq) {
     auto * sctx = (llama_sampler_dist *) smpl->ctx;
 
-    const bool res = llama_sampler_backend_support(smpl, buft);
+    // Diagnostic gate: keep the GPU sampler prefix through top-k/top-p but let the
+    // tiny final distribution run on the CPU. This isolates the unexpectedly costly
+    // dist_sampled_token GET_ROWS without changing the preceding candidate selection.
+    const bool force_cpu_dist = std::getenv("LLAMA_DIST_CPU") != nullptr;
+    const bool res = !force_cpu_dist && llama_sampler_backend_support(smpl, buft);
 
     sctx->init(res);
     sctx->backend_transactional = n_outputs_max_per_seq > 1;
